# Game end: leftover sticks awarded to 1st, tie-break by starting seat, and oka/uma
# adjusted scores — ruleset difference (engine.md §5 step 5, rules.md §1 uma/oka/tie_break_order).
# South 4, dealer=3, sticks=2 (2000 on table), scores: 35000 24000 24000 15000.
# Exhaustive draw with 0 tenpai -> dealer Seat 3 does not repeat; Seat 0 >= 30000 -> game ends!
# Leftover 2 sticks (+2000) go to 1st place (Seat 0) -> final_scores: 37000 24000 24000 15000.
# Seat 1 and Seat 2 tie at 24000 -> starting seat order (0 > 1 > 2 > 3) gives final_ranks: 0 1 2 3.
# Adjusted scores (raw integer points = final_score - return + oka + uma*1000):
# - Mahjong Soul (return=25000, oka=0, uma=[+15, +5, -5, -15]):
#   * Seat 0 (1st): 37000 - 25000 + 0 + 15000 = +27000
#   * Seat 1 (2nd): 24000 - 25000 + 0 +  5000 =  +4000
#   * Seat 2 (3rd): 24000 - 25000 + 0 -  5000 =  -6000
#   * Seat 3 (4th): 15000 - 25000 + 0 - 15000 = -25000
# - Tenhou (return=30000, oka=+20000 to 1st, uma=[+20, +10, -10, -20]):
#   * Seat 0 (1st): 37000 - 30000 + 20000 + 20000 = +47000
#   * Seat 1 (2nd): 24000 - 30000 +     0 + 10000 =  +4000
#   * Seat 2 (3rd): 24000 - 30000 +     0 - 10000 = -16000
#   * Seat 3 (4th): 15000 - 30000 +     0 - 20000 = -35000

[meta]
name: endgame_oka_uma_tiebreak
title: Game end awards leftover sticks to 1st, breaks ties by seat, and applies ruleset oka and uma
rules: both
source: engine.md §5 step 5, rules.md §1 (uma, oka, tie_break_order, endgame_riichi_sticks)

[round]
game_length: south
wind: S
round: 4
honba: 0
sticks: 2
dealer: 3
scores: 35000 24000 24000 15000

